# Question bank review (Set A)

Tick an item to approve it: change `- [ ]` to `- [x]`, then rerun `eval\build_bank.py`.
`BLOCK` flags keep an item unverified even if ticked (ask Claude to redraft it). `warn` flags are for you to judge: a tick overrides them.
To reject an item, leave it unticked and write a note under it.

## Misconception names (FR / AR drafted by LLM)

- [ ] names:M1
  - EN: Adds numerators and adds denominators
  - FR: Additionne les numérateurs et additionne les dénominateurs
  - AR: يضيف البسط ويضيف المقام
  - description: To add two fractions, the student adds the tops and adds the bottoms: a/b + c/d = (a+c)/(b+d).
  - contrast example: 1/2 + 1/2 would give 2/4 = 1/2, but two halves make one whole, so 1/2 + 1/2 = 1.
  - MAP label `Adding_across` (307 rows), Eedi IDs [217]

- [ ] names:M2
  - EN: Multiplies both numerator and denominator by the whole number
  - FR: Multiplie le numérateur et le dénominateur par le nombre entier
  - AR: يضرب كل من البسط والمقام في العدد الكامل
  - description: To multiply a fraction by a whole number, the student multiplies the top and the bottom: k × a/b = (ka)/(kb).
  - contrast example: 2 × 1/2 would give 2/4 = 1/2, but two halves make one whole, so 2 × 1/2 = 1.
  - MAP label `Duplication` (704 rows), Eedi IDs [1976]

- [ ] names:M3
  - EN: Thinks 'two negatives make a positive' always applies
  - FR: Pense que « deux négatifs font un positif » s'applique toujours
  - AR: يعتقد أن « سالبين يصنعان موجبًا » ينطبق دائمًا
  - description: When a calculation has two minus signs, the student makes the answer positive, e.g. (-8) - (-5) = 3 or 13.
  - contrast example: (-2) - (-1): start at -2 and remove a debt of 1, you get -1, which is still negative.
  - MAP label `Positive` (566 rows), Eedi IDs [1435, 795]

- [ ] names:M4
  - EN: Makes equivalent fractions by adding instead of multiplying
  - FR: Forme des fractions équivalentes en additionnant au lieu de multiplier
  - AR: يُنشئ كسورًا مكافئة عن طريق الجمع بدلاً من الضرب
  - description: To find an equivalent fraction, the student adds the same number to the top and bottom instead of multiplying.
  - contrast example: 1/2 -> add 1 to top and bottom -> 2/3, but 2/3 is bigger than 1/2; 1/2 = 2/4 (multiply by 2).
  - MAP label `Additive` (929 rows), Eedi IDs [1429]

## Questions and hints

Answer keys and option mappings come from the data (MAP labels or Eedi labels), not the LLM.

- [ ] Q1  (MAP 33472, target M1)
  - Q: 1/3+2/5=
